<title>UK: CIBC ADDS 20 BILLION YEN TO THREE-YEAR FRN.</title>
<headline>CIBC ADDS 20 BILLION YEN TO THREE-YEAR FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following floating-rate issue has been increased to 50 billion yen from 30 billion yen, lead manager Tokyo-Mitsubishi International said on Monday.</p>
<p>All terms remain the same.</p>
<p> BORROWER   CANADIAN IMPERIAL BANK OF COMMERCE</p>
<p> AMT    *50 BLN YEN   BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY    22.AUG.00</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN     -12.5 BP  PAY DATE    22.AUG.97</p>
<p> MOODY	AA3	 ISS PRICE  PAR	 FULL FEES   0.125</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA-	 REOFFER    PAR</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS (M) 1	 SALE LIMITS US/GB/JP/CA</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ONTARIO   HOME CTRY  CANADA    TAX PROVS   GROSS-UP</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.05	SELL CONC  0.075     PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> NOTES     *LAUNCHED ORIGINALLY FOR 30 BILLION YEN ON 08.AUG.97.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
